# Frontend Theme And Responsive Rule

- Use this palette by default for new frontend UI work:
  - Primary: `#276bd0`
  - Accent: `#d69e00`
  - Base light theme: `#ffffff`
- Prefer light surfaces, high contrast text, and keep interactive states readable.
- Reuse theme tokens from `frontend/src/index.css`; avoid hardcoding random colors.

# Responsive Requirement (Mandatory)

- Every frontend change must be reviewed for 4 device groups:
  - Mobile small (Galaxy Fold width range)
  - Mobile standard
  - Tablet
  - Desktop/Web
- Avoid fixed widths that break narrow screens.
- Use responsive Tailwind classes (`sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`) and fluid spacing.
- Ensure touch targets are usable on mobile (buttons/inputs not cramped).
- Keep forms and key actions visible without horizontal scroll.

# Implementation Checklist

- [ ] Uses project palette tokens or the approved hex colors above
- [ ] Verified layout in small mobile width (Galaxy Fold class)
- [ ] Verified layout in mobile/tablet/desktop breakpoints
- [ ] No horizontal overflow introduced
